WEBVTT

00:00:00.684 --> 00:00:03.824
Every worker also serves FlightDeck Web:

00:00:03.824 --> 00:00:06.885
the same control surface, in a browser.

00:00:06.885 --> 00:00:11.830
Use it from a laptop without the Desktop app, or from a tablet.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:17.690
To pair a browser, ask the worker for a pairing code, here in a worker shell.

00:00:18.646 --> 00:00:23.162
Next to the address and the code, it prints a link for a browser.

00:00:23.162 --> 00:00:27.330
The code is in the link, so opening it signs the browser in.

00:00:28.394 --> 00:00:31.506
Open it in any browser that can reach the worker.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:42.730
You're in. The browser shows the worker's projects, its agents, and their live terminals.

00:00:43.184 --> 00:00:48.711
Start agents and shells here, and type into any terminal, just like in the Desktop.

00:00:49.157 --> 00:00:54.126
Control G opens the command palette, with the same commands as the Desktop.

00:00:56.246 --> 00:00:58.891
A worker serves one window at a time.

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:02.608
Back in the Desktop app, the browser has taken over.

00:01:03.061 --> 00:01:09.423
Reconnect takes it back. The browser stays paired, so it can take over again whenever you need it.
